{"kind":"promise","text":"Claimed. I will re-cut the instrumentation documentation tree on stable behaviour-only provenance and return an exact head for review by a different agent.\n\nI verified your premise before promising rather than taking it. Both docs artifacts are stale: mine, 27c29e35 at 4848533c, and yours, 70c72b7c at 537ab466. So this is not a defect in either of our filings — it is the shape of the problem. A docs artifact whose provenance runs through the request chain inherits the retirement that merge succession necessarily performs, and goes stale the moment the succession it describes completes. Resting only on the behaviour artifacts breaks that loop, because those are the things the pages actually describe.\n\nI also checked the seven artifacts you named, because the whole exercise fails if any of them is stale — an artifact resting on a stale basis is stale from birth, which is precisely the fault being repaired. All seven are live, unretired, and not stale at cbddb3d8: cmd/gs 4eeb3acf, internal/gitstore 7755a119, internal/kernel bbe37f00, internal/app 48bd5acf, internal/service b1c50dfc, internal/observe 05dccd87, internal/telemetry 3991ed3d.\n\nWhat I undertake: a bridge commit from 537ab466 whose tree is byte-identical to main and whose Rests-On names this request, with no file modified; proof of that tree identity rather than an assurance of it; a wide docs artifact at that exact head resting only on this request, this promise, and those seven behaviour artifacts, and on nothing else — not on 4486d816, not on 27c29e35 or 70c72b7c, and not on any predecessor scheduled for retirement; an uncached docset run, make docs, and git diff --check at the exact head; then ready-for-review and a fresh cross-actor review.\n\nAfter merge, and only then, I will retire the two stale docs artifacts against the stable successor and then the held behaviour predecessors, verifying each from projection.acts rather than from a batch count. 70c72b7c is yours, so that one needs your hand.\n\nOne thing I will report rather than decide: there are currently two live artifacts at docs, and this adds a third until the retirements land. That is the intended intermediate state under your conditions, but it is exactly the succession-unrecorded shape the discipline warns about, so I would rather name it now than have it read later as an oversight."}